     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"answer\":\"None of the recalls listed in this case covers the owner's reported rear-camera failure from wires damaged during normal tailgate use. Those recalls address hood-latch separation, tonneau-cover panel separation, fuel-pump feed-port cracking, and improperly manufactured seat rivets—not rear-camera wiring. This explains the lack of a match in the supplied record; the records do not explain why Honda had not issued a recall for the reported camera failure.\",\"scope\":\"answered\",\"recheck\":false,\"citations\":[{\"kind\":\"complaint\",\"id\":\"11443328\",\"quote\":\"normal tailgate use pinches the wires and eventually they become damaged, severing the connection and disabling the rear camera\"},{\"kind\":\"recall\",\"id\":\"21V932000\",\"quote\":\"The hood latch striker may become damaged and separate from the hood\"},{\"kind\":\"recall\",\"id\":\"20E068000\",\"quote\":\"possibly allowing the rear panel to separate from the vehicle\"},{\"kind\":\"recall\",\"id\":\"19V053000\",\"quote\":\"can result in the fuel pump feed port cracking\"},{\"kind\":\"recall\",\"id\":\"18V221000\",\"quote\":\"may have been assembled with improperly manufactured rivets\"}]}",
